# Knowledge

What building {{name}} taught: one entry per reusable pattern, pitfall, or replaced approach. Search it (and
`.operonx/catalog.md`, every op, graph and job) before writing something new. When a pattern changes, edit
its entry; never add a second one.

An entry, newest last:

```text
### K1 · retry the TTS call twice · pattern
where: src/speech/ops.py
use: a provider call that times out now and then: `@op(retry=2)`, not a loop in the op
```

A pitfall's `use` starts with the symptom, so a search for it finds the entry. A `replaced` entry adds
`instead:` (what to use now). `operonx lint` warns when a `where` file is gone.
